# Intake disposition intent-frame fix — apply ladder

The acceptance-smoke rerun11 inverted variant A again — but on a NEW shape the
#173 word-boundary fix did not cover: "I want to stop doing it by hand
completely" read START because the "want to" START tell appeared BEFORE the
"stop" STOP tell (earliest-wins), so the intent-frame beat the cessation verb
it governs.

A CLEAR-DIRECTION fix: an intent-frame ("want to / need to / 'd love to / 'd
like to / have to / trying to") governing a stop-verb ("stop / quit / avoid /
cut out / drop / get rid of / hand off / offload") is a STOP at the frame
position; and the bare "want to / need to" START tells carry a NEGATIVE
LOOKAHEAD so they do NOT fire when the frame governs a cessation verb. Genuine
STARTs ("I want to start journaling", "I need to begin reviewing") still read
START.

